Follow the platform APIs that moved out from under it

Counting rather than crashing one screen at a time: every android.* and
vendor.* member the app names was checked against the boot classpath the
device actually runs - thirty jars, apexes included, superclasses followed.
Nine of seventeen thousand did not resolve.

Four are the same call under a new spelling, and are rewritten as such:

  ServiceState.getRadioTechnology      -> getRilVoiceRadioTechnology
  SmsManager.getServiceCenterAddress   -> getSmscAddress
  SmsManager.setServiceCenterAddress   -> setSmscAddress
  TelephonyManager.getIccOperatorNumericForData -> getSimOperatorNumeric

The rest are gone with nothing to put in their place.
SurfaceControl.screenshot returns null, which the caller already logs as
"Failed to take screenshot" and carries on from. BluetoothAdapter.clearBleApps
drops out; so do LG's own Window.addBypassKeyFlags and
Window.setMiniActivityFullScreen, and the bypassKeyFlags field they go with -
fifteen read-modify-writes of a field nothing here reads, which is how the
test screens used to swallow the hardware keys. The keys now behave normally,
which is easier to leave a test screen with, not harder.

